{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":31577,"num_turns":7,"result":"Fixed. `semver.py` now implements full SemVer 2.0.0 ordering:\n\n- `parse` validates against the official SemVer regex and returns `(major, minor, patch, prerelease)`, raising `ValueError` for malformed input like `\"1.2\"`, `\"a.b.c\"`, `\"v1.2.3\"`, or leading zeros.\n- `compare` compares the numeric triple, then the pre-release per spec rule 11: a version with a pre-release ranks below one without, numeric identifiers (`beta.2 < beta.11`) compare numerically and rank below alphanumeric ones (`alpha < alpha.1 < alpha.beta < beta`), and a longer identifier list wins on equal prefixes.\n- Build metadata (`+build.5`) is stripped before comparison, so `1.0.0+build.5 == 1.0.0`.\n- `sort_versions` uses the same ordering via a `_sort_key` helper that encodes identifiers uniformly so mixed int/str comparisons never raise `TypeError`.\n\nValidation: the 2 existing tests pass, plus a scripted check of every bullet in the issue (the `1.10.0` case, the full spec example chain, build-metadata equality, sorting with pre-releases, and 9 malformed inputs raising `ValueError`). Tests directory untouched.","session_id":"5030c00c-6e0c-4ab2-b082-e3a8b3d1ea2f","usage":{"input_tokens":3444,"output_tokens":2766,"cache_read_input_tokens":70656,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"factory_credits":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"ttft_ms":1313.2857142857142}}
